Package: lcos-base
Version: 1.0.0-2
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Installed-Size: 192
Maintainer: LCOS <lcos@lunduke.com>
Homepage: https://lunduke.com
Depends: lcos-archive-keyring (>= 0.7), lcos-branding (>= 0.9-1), eject, cifs-utils, keyutils, gvfs-backends, dialog, xfce4-screensaver, xarchiver, thunar-archive-plugin, exfatprogs, xdg-desktop-portal-gtk, fonts-noto-color-emoji, firmware-iwlwifi, firmware-intel-sound, firmware-intel-graphics, fwupd, thermald, iio-sensor-proxy, switcheroo-control, ipp-usb, sane-airscan, intel-media-va-driver, zstd, console-setup, at-spi2-core, 7zip, x11-utils, libnss-mdns, system-config-printer, cups-pk-helper, fdisk, ntfs-3g, libmtp-runtime, gdebi, usbutils
Replaces: base-files
Description: LCOS 1.0.0 identity, GRUB drop-in, X/boot-order system config
 os-release / issue for LCOS 1.0.0 (excalibur), lcos-write-os-release,
 and /etc/default/grub.d/lcos.cfg (BACKGROUND lcos-splash-1024x768.png,
 GFXMODE=1024x768, GFXPAYLOAD keep, CMDLINE_LINUX_DEFAULT quiet splash
 loglevel=2).
 .
 AMD GPUs (0.9.2-2, #115/#118): no Xorg driver override. Xorg
 autoselects the AMD driver as in 0.8. The 0.9/0.9.1 modesetting snippets,
 /etc/init.d/lcos-amdgpu-ddx and /usr/lib/lcos/lcos-amdgpu-ddx are removed
 on upgrade.
 .
 insserv overrides so LightDM starts after elogind/seatd
 and /etc/init.d/plymouth no longer quits Plymouth at boot (LightDM is the
 single Plymouth quitter; the shutdown splash is kept).
 .
 Depends on the overlay keyring and branding artwork.
 0.9.1: recommends eject (#104) and cifs-utils + keyutils (#111). From
 0.9.1-3 they are Recommends, not Depends, so the Updates tool's plain
 apt-get upgrade moves 0.8 systems without holding lcos-base back.
 0.9.2-4: eject, cifs-utils, keyutils and gvfs-backends (Thunar SMB
 browsing) are Depends again; 0.9.2-5 adds dialog (debconf frontend,
 #125). Updates 0.9.2-2+ installs kept-back
 upgrades that only add packages, so upgraders receive them.
 0.9.3-1: ships /etc/apt/preferences.d/lcos-amd-backports.pref (not a
 conffile) with i386 Mesa pinned to excalibur-backports too (#129).
 0.9.3-2: Depends xfce4-screensaver (screen lock on lid close/suspend,
 #109), xarchiver + thunar-archive-plugin (archive manager, #132) and
 exfatprogs (exFAT tools, #131) so upgraders get the 0.9.3 ISO additions.
 0.9.3-3: Depends xdg-desktop-portal-gtk (pulls xdg-desktop-portal) so
 Chromium/Brave file pickers work (#135).
 0.9.4-2: the apt pin also takes firmware-realtek from excalibur-backports
 (newest rtw89 firmware for LLK lcos22 Realtek USB Wi-Fi, #138).
 0.9.4-3: ships /usr/lib/sysctl.d/99-lcos-userns.conf
 (user.max_user_namespaces=15000) so Steam, Flatpak and bubblewrap work;
 it overrides the =0 line older ISOs left in /etc/sysctl.d.
 0.9.4-4: Depends fonts-noto-color-emoji (colour emoji, #142) so
 upgraders get the 0.9.4 ISO addition.
 0.9.4-5: Ubuntu 26.10 hardware gap — Depends firmware-iwlwifi,
 firmware-intel-sound, firmware-intel-graphics (backports 20260810),
 fwupd, thermald, iio-sensor-proxy, switcheroo-control, ipp-usb,
 sane-airscan, intel-media-va-driver. Ships sysvinit wrappers for
 thermald, iio-sensor-proxy, switcheroo-control and ipp-usb (Debian
 packages are systemd-only). firmware-sof-signed stays at 2025.01-1
 (no newer build in excalibur-backports). Apt pin updated for the
 three firmware packages.
 0.9.4-6: Depends zstd and console-setup (kernel#15: initramfs "No zstd"
 and "setupcon is missing" warnings on kernel upgrades), at-spi2-core
 (accessibility bus, #117) and 7zip (#116) so upgraders get the 0.9.4
 ISO additions.
 0.9.4-7: ships /etc/X11/Xsession.d/20lcos-atspi-reset, which drops a
 stale AT_SPI_BUS root-window property left by the LightDM greeter's
 at-spi bus (lightdm uid) so session apps reach the user's own
 accessibility bus after a greeter login; Depends x11-utils (xprop).
 0.9.5-1: dpkg file trigger (/boot, /lib/modules, /lib/firmware and
 /usr variants) runs /usr/lib/lcos/lcos-reboot-required, which writes
 /var/run/reboot-required and appends to /var/run/reboot-required.pkgs
 after linux-image-*, firmware-*, intel-microcode or amd64-microcode is
 installed or upgraded (same-version kernels included), so Updates offers
 a restart (review r15 U-1).
 0.9.5-2: /lib/lsb/init-functions.d/05-lcos-home unsets the kernel's
 HOME=/ for sysvinit boot services, so lightdm and NetworkManager no
 longer create /.cache at boot (#112); postinst removes an empty /.cache
 and any Mesa shader cache left there.
 0.9.5-3: same content as 0.9.5-2, rebuilt on the 0.9.5 track reset
 to the 0.9.4 release (0.9.5-1 and 0.9.5-2 were tagged before the
 reset).
 0.9.5-4: printing. Depends libnss-mdns (resolve <printer>.local),
 system-config-printer (Print Settings) and cups-pk-helper, so upgraders
 get the 0.9.5 ISO additions (Updates installs with Recommends off). On
 upgrade from below 0.9.5-4, postinst adds existing sudo-group users
 (UID 1000-59999) to lpadmin once; installers before 0.9.5 left them out,
 so adding a printer failed with CUPS 'forbidden'. Postinst diverts
 /etc/xdg/autostart/print-applet.desktop (system-config-printer) to the
 name print-applet.desktop.distrib and installs a Hidden=true copy from
 /usr/share/lcos-base, so the print-queue tray icon is off by default and
 can be turned on in Session and Startup.
 0.9.5-5: Depends fdisk (the installer's autoremove purged it on every
 install since 0.9.2, so upgraders get it back) and ships the conffile
 /etc/apt/apt.conf.d/02lcos-neverautoremove: APT::NeverAutoRemove for
 fdisk and the core Xfce desktop (xfce4-panel, xfwm4, xfce4-session,
 xfdesktop4, xfce4-settings, xfconf, thunar, network-manager-applet,
 nm-connection-editor), so removing the xfce4 metapackage no longer makes
 autoremove offer the desktop.
 0.9.5-6: GRUB drop-in sets GRUB_DISABLE_OS_PROBER=false, so update-grub
 lists Windows and other installed systems (GRUB 2.12 skips os-prober by
 default). Depends ntfs-3g (ntfsresize, ntfsfix; only a udisks2 Recommends
 before). On upgrade from below 0.9.5-6, postinst removes the bake-only
 /etc/apt/apt.conf.d/00lcos-noninteractive (APT::Get::Assume-Yes) when it
 is unchanged from what the images shipped, so terminal apt asks before
 installing or removing again; an edited copy is kept.
 0.9.6-1: Recommends libmtp-runtime (mtp-probe, called by the
 libmtp-common udev rule; only a libmtp9t64 Recommends, so images built
 with --apt-recommends false logged "mtp-probe" errors and missed MTP
 devices not in libmtp's list). Editor 2026-10-22. Identity stays 0.9.5.
 0.9.6-2: identity 0.9.6 (os-release, /usr/lib/os-release, issue,
 issue.net, lcos-write-os-release). libmtp-runtime moves from Recommends
 to Depends so upgraders get it (Updates installs with Recommends off).
 Editor 2026-10-22.
 0.9.6-3: Depends gdebi (graphical .deb installer; lcos-desktop-config
 0.9.6-1 makes it the default for .deb files) so upgraders get the 0.9.6
 ISO addition (Updates installs with Recommends off). Editor 2026-10-23.
 0.9.7-1: version bump for LCOS 0.9.7; identity 0.9.7 (os-release,
 /usr/lib/os-release, issue, issue.net, lcos-write-os-release). Depends
 unchanged from 0.9.6-3. Editor 2026-10-24.
 1.0.0-1: version bump for LCOS 1.0.0; identity 1.0.0 (os-release,
 /usr/lib/os-release, issue, issue.net, lcos-write-os-release). Depends
 unchanged from 0.9.7-1. Editor 2026-10-27.
 1.0.0-2: Depends usbutils (lsusb, #176) so upgraders get the 1.0.0
 ISO addition (Updates installs with Recommends off). Identity stays
 1.0.0. Editor 2026-10-27.
 Postinst re-applies identity on configure so apt upgrades overwrite
 stale 0.4 conffile text kept by noninteractive Updates.
